republic-function.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P5 (S16): "well" is taken as faring well, being blessed and happy in P5 and as performing the soul's function of living excellently where just_lives_well is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C2 (S18) does not follow (republic-function.logic.r3.sense1)
republic-function.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C2 (S18): just_happy = F, just_lives_well = T, just_lives_well_2 = F, unjust_lives_ill = T, unjust_miserable = T
republic-function.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P5 (S16): "ill" is taken as faring badly, being miserable in P5 and as performing the soul's function of living badly where unjust_lives_ill is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C2 (S18) does not follow (republic-function.logic.r3.sense2)
republic-function.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C2 (S18): just_happy = T, just_lives_well = T, unjust_lives_ill = T, unjust_lives_ill_2 = F, unjust_miserable = F
